{"name":"Electromagnetic","hex":"#2e3840","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"electromagnetic","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Relating to electromagnetism."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/electromagnetic"}],"entries":[{"title":"Electromagnetism","blocks":[{"text":"In physics, electromagnetism is an interaction that occurs between particles with electric charge via electromagnetic fields. The electromagnetic force is one of the four fundamental forces of nature. It is the dominant force in the interactions of atoms and molecules. Electromagnetism describes and relates the three distinct but closely intertwined phenomena of electricity, magnetism, and optics. In the study of electromagnetism these phenomena are described by the 3 sub-disciplines: electrostatics, magnetostatics, and electrodynamics."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/VFPt_Solenoid_correct2.svg/330px-VFPt_Solenoid_correct2.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electromagnetism"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Plasma_globe_60th.jpg/500px-Plasma_globe_60th.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Plasma_globe_60th.jpg/1280px-Plasma_globe_60th.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Plasma_globe_60th.jpg/500px-Plasma_globe_60th.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Electromagnetic interactions are responsible for the glowing filaments in this plasma globe.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APlasma_globe_60th.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Cat_demonstrating_static_cling_with_styrofoam_peanuts.jpg/330px-Cat_demonstrating_static_cling_with_styrofoam_peanuts.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Cat_demonstrating_static_cling_with_styrofoam_peanuts.jpg/330px-Cat_demonstrating_static_cling_with_styrofoam_peanuts.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Foam peanuts clinging to a cat's fur due to static electricity. The cat's fur becomes charged due to the triboelectric effect. The electric field of the charged fur causes polarization of the molecules of the foam due to electrostatic induction, resulting in a slight attraction of the light plastic pieces to the fur.[8][9][10][11] This effect is also the cause of static cling in clothes.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACat_demonstrating_static_cling_with_styrofoam_peanuts.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/A_Treatise_on_Electricity_and_Magnetism_Volume_2_003.jpg/500px-A_Treatise_on_Electricity_and_Magnetism_Volume_2_003.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/A_Treatise_on_Electricity_and_Magnetism_Volume_2_003.jpg/500px-A_Treatise_on_Electricity_and_Magnetism_Volume_2_003.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cover of A Treatise on Electricity and Magnetism","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AA_Treatise_on_Electricity_and_Magnetism_Volume_2_003.jpg"}],"sounds":{"electromagnetic":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/89/Electromagnetic.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/8/89/Electromagnetic.ogg/Electromagnetic.ogg.mp3"}]}}}